  "segment_count": 324,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 9.27,
      "end": 9.28,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Hi everyone. Welcome back."
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 9.28,
      "end": 10.67,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "So today I'd like to look at a problem"
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 10.68,
      "end": 13.07,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "on manipulating Fourier series."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 13.08,
      "end": 15.11,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "Specifically, we're asked to find the"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 15.12,
      "end": 18.75,
      "duration": 3.63,
      "text": "Fourier series of cosine t or 2t minus"
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 18.76,
      "end": 20.91,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "pi over 4."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 20.92,
      "end": 22.79,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "And then the second problem is given a"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 22.8,
      "end": 24.31,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "square wave function, which takes on the"
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 24.32,
      "end": 26.95,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "value of minus one and one, and it's"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 26.96,
      "end": 28.71,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "2 pi periodic."
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 28.72,
      "end": 29.99,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "We're also told that the square wave"
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 30.0,
      "end": 31.79,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "function has the Fourier series 4 over"
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 31.8,
      "end": 35.51,
      "duration": 3.71,
      "text": "pi 1 over n sin nt."
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 35.52,
      "end": 37.55,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "And the question is to find the Fourier"
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 37.56,
      "end": 39.75,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "series of three related functions."
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 39.76,
      "end": 41.27,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "So the first function takes on the value"
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 41.28,
      "end": 42.87,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "of zero and four"
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 42.88,
      "end": 44.71,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "on the intervals minus pi to zero and"
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 44.72,
      "end": 45.91,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "zero to pi."
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 45.92,
      "end": 47.55,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "Note that this function is also 2 pi"
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 47.56,
      "end": 49.39,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "periodic."
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 49.4,
      "end": 51.79,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "The second problem is"
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 51.8,
      "end": 53.47,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "to find the Fourier series of a function"
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 53.48,
      "end": 55.83,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "which is minus one from minus one to"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 55.84,
      "end": 59.11,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "zero, and one from zero to one."
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 59.12,
      "end": 60.67,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "So this is the square wave function, but"
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 60.68,
      "end": 63.67,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "now has period two."
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 63.68,
      "end": 65.27,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "And then lastly, we're asked to find the"
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 65.28,
      "end": 67.43,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "Fourier series of a function f of t"
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 67.44,
      "end": 69.79,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "which is absolute t."
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 69.8,
      "end": 71.51,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "And it's defined as absolute t on the"
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 71.52,
      "end": 74.27,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "interval from minus pi to pi."
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 74.28,
      "end": 76.11,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "However, this function f is going to be"
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 76.12,
      "end": 78.15,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "extended on the entire domain with"
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 78.16,
      "end": 79.95,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "period 2 pi."
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 79.96,
      "end": 80.95,
      "duration": 0.99,
      "text": "Okay, so I'll let you think about this"
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 80.96,
      "end": 94.23,
      "duration": 13.27,
      "text": "problem, and I'll be back in a moment."
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 96.27,
      "end": 96.28,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Hi everyone. Welcome back."
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 96.28,
      "end": 97.63,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "Okay, so let's take a look at the first"
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 97.64,
      "end": 99.99,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "problem, finding the Fourier series of"
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 100.0,
      "end": 102.07,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "cosine 2t"
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 102.08,
      "end": 108.79,
      "duration": 6.71,
      "text": "minus pi over 4."
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 110.31,
      "end": 110.32,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So in this class, when we say find the"
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 110.32,
      "end": 111.67,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "Fourier series, what we're really"
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 111.68,
      "end": 113.07,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "looking for"
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 113.08,
      "end": 115.71,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "are coefficients"
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 115.72,
      "end": 121.15,
      "duration": 5.43,
      "text": "a0, an, and bn"
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 124.67,
      "end": 124.68,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "such that for example, we can write"
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 124.68,
      "end": 127.07,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "our function out"
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 127.08,
      "end": 129.669,
      "duration": 2.589,
      "text": "as a sum of sines and cosines with these"
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 129.679,
      "end": 132.43,
      "duration": 2.751,
      "text": "values an and bn."
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 132.44,
      "end": 133.43,
      "duration": 0.99,
      "text": "Now"
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 133.44,
      "end": 134.59,
      "duration": 1.15,
      "text": "what we could do is we could take this"
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 134.6,
      "end": 136.19,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "function, plug it into the integral"
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 136.2,
      "end": 137.99,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "formulas, and compute using the"
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 138.0,
      "end": 142.07,
      "duration": 4.07,
      "text": "integrals the value a0, an, and bn."
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 142.08,
      "end": 143.59,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "However, there's a bit of a trick, and"
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 143.6,
      "end": 145.35,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "that's to realize"
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 145.36,
      "end": 147.59,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "that this function cosine 2t minus pi"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 147.6,
      "end": 149.11,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "over 4"
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 149.12,
      "end": 153.43,
      "duration": 4.31,
      "text": "it's really just a sinusoidal function"
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 153.44,
      "end": 155.95,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "and it's currently in an amplitude phase"
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 155.96,
      "end": 157.27,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "form."
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 157.28,
      "end": 159.35,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "And we can always convert an amplitude"
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 159.36,
      "end": 161.79,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "phase form of a sinusoidal function"
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 161.8,
      "end": 164.39,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "into some amplitude times a sine and"
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 164.4,
      "end": 165.91,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "some amplitude"
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 165.92,
      "end": 167.31,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "times a cosine"
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 167.32,
      "end": 170.55,
      "duration": 3.23,
      "text": "and add the two up. So"
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 170.56,
      "end": 173.51,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "specifically"
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 175.99,
      "end": 176.0,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "this can be done by"
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 176.0,
      "end": 177.31,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "recalling"
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 177.32,
      "end": 179.83,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "the cosine identity"
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 179.84,
      "end": 184.79,
      "duration": 4.95,
      "text": "cosine a minus b"
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 187.71,
      "end": 187.72,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "is cosine a times cosine b"
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 187.72,
      "end": 189.91,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "plus"
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 189.92,
      "end": 191.19,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "sin of a"
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 191.2,
      "end": 194.79,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "sin of b."
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 197.19,
      "end": 197.2,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And if we identify a with 2t and b with"
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 197.2,
      "end": 202.55,
      "duration": 5.35,
      "text": "pi over 4"
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 210.23,
      "end": 210.24,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "is cosine 2t"
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 210.24,
      "end": 212.95,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "cosine pi over 4"
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 212.96,
      "end": 216.71,
      "duration": 3.75,
      "text": "plus sin 2t"
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 223.95,
      "end": 223.96,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And now sin of t uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 223.96,
      "end": 226.95,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "pi over 4 and cosine pi over 4 are both"
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 226.96,
      "end": 234.59,
      "duration": 7.63,
      "text": "1 over root 2."
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 238.07,
      "end": 238.08,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So f of t f of t becomes 1 over root 2"
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 238.08,
      "end": 241.75,
      "duration": 3.67,
      "text": "cosine 2t"
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 249.95,
      "end": 249.96,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And that's it."
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 249.96,
      "end": 251.15,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "So when we take a look at this"
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 251.16,
      "end": 253.11,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "expression for f of t"
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 253.12,
      "end": 254.87,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "we see that this is actually in exactly"
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 254.88,
      "end": 256.39,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "the same form"
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 256.4,
      "end": 257.789,
      "duration": 1.389,
      "text": "that we started or that we were seeking"
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 257.799,
      "end": 259.03,
      "duration": 1.231,
      "text": "in the beginning, the Fourier series"
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 259.04,
      "end": 261.71,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "representation for f."
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 261.72,
      "end": 263.39,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "So this is this is the end of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 263.4,
      "end": 264.63,
      "duration": 1.23,
      "text": "problem."
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 264.64,
      "end": 265.95,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "We don't have to actually compute any"
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 265.96,
      "end": 268.75,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "integrals."
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 270.31,
      "end": 270.32,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay, so now let's take a look at part"
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 270.32,
      "end": 273.15,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "two."
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 274.79,
      "end": 274.8,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So for part two, we're asked to find the"
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 274.8,
      "end": 276.11,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "Fourier series"
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 276.12,
      "end": 278.23,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "of several different functions"
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 278.24,
      "end": 289.43,
      "duration": 11.19,
      "text": "and I'll just take a look at part one."
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 296.87,
      "end": 296.88,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So in this case"
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 296.88,
      "end": 298.79,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "f of t takes on the value of zero from"
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 298.8,
      "end": 300.63,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "minus pi to zero"
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 300.64,
      "end": 303.51,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "and the value of four from zero to pi."
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 303.52,
      "end": 304.83,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "And if I were to quickly sketch this"
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 304.84,
      "end": 315.19,
      "duration": 10.35,
      "text": "function"
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 320.91,
      "end": 320.92,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "zero"
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 320.92,
      "end": 323.55,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "pi minus pi"
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 323.56,
      "end": 330.03,
      "duration": 6.47,
      "text": "This is f of t."
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 332.63,
      "end": 332.64,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And we see that it's actually related"
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 332.64,
      "end": 336.99,
      "duration": 4.35,
      "text": "I can draw in dashes just to be clear"
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 337.0,
      "end": 338.67,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "what the original square wave function"
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 338.68,
      "end": 339.99,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "might look like."
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 340.0,
      "end": 345.35,
      "duration": 5.35,
      "text": "So this is square wave of t."
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 346.31,
      "end": 346.32,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "We see that if we were to take the"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 346.32,
      "end": 347.83,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "square wave function"
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 347.84,
      "end": 350.03,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "and shift it up"
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 350.04,
      "end": 351.59,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "the square wave takes on values of plus"
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 351.6,
      "end": 353.35,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "one and minus one. But if we take the"
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 353.36,
      "end": 355.11,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "square wave function and shift it up one"
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 355.12,
      "end": 356.19,
      "duration": 1.07,
      "text": "unit"
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 356.2,
      "end": 357.99,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "and then rescale it"
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 358.0,
      "end": 359.51,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "we'll then get the function we're"
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "start": 359.52,
      "end": 362.35,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "looking for f of t."
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "start": 362.36,
      "end": 364.31,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "So specifically"
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "start": 364.32,
      "end": 365.75,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "we can write f of t in terms of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 365.76,
      "end": 367.19,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "square wave"
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 367.2,
      "end": 368.51,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "as"
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 368.52,
      "end": 370.03,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "well, we have to shift the square wave"
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 370.04,
      "end": 374.03,
      "duration": 3.99,
      "text": "function up one."
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 375.39,
      "end": 375.4,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And then we have to amplify it by a"
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 375.4,
      "end": 377.83,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "factor of two."
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 377.84,
      "end": 379.15,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "So then when we seek the Fourier series"
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 379.16,
      "end": 381.19,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "for f all we have to do is substitute"
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 381.2,
      "end": 382.47,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "the Fourier series for the square wave"
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 382.48,
      "end": 386.59,
      "duration": 4.11,
      "text": "function in."
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 388.55,
      "end": 388.56,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay, so let's do this. So we have 1"
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 388.56,
      "end": 390.35,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "plus"
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 390.36,
      "end": 393.59,
      "duration": 3.23,
      "text": "4 over pi."
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 395.07,
      "end": 395.08,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So I'm writing here this Fourier series"
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 395.08,
      "end": 397.47,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "for the square wave function."
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 397.48,
      "end": 400.11,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "n odd"
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 400.12,
      "end": 402.51,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "1 over n"
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 402.52,
      "end": 408.95,
      "duration": 6.43,
      "text": "sin nt."
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 410.75,
      "end": 410.76,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So by manipulating the Fourier series"
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 410.76,
      "end": 413.59,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "for the square wave function"
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 413.6,
      "end": 418.23,
      "duration": 4.63,
      "text": "we can arrive at a Fourier series"
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 423.39,
      "end": 423.4,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "n odd"
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 423.4,
      "end": 426.03,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "1 over n"
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 426.04,
      "end": 429.51,
      "duration": 3.47,
      "text": "sin nt."
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 437.59,
      "end": 437.6,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "The second function f"
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 437.6,
      "end": 438.67,
      "duration": 1.07,
      "text": "t"
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 438.68,
      "end": 440.79,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "I'll just rewrite it again."
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 440.8,
      "end": 443.27,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "f of t takes on the value of"
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 443.28,
      "end": 446.75,
      "duration": 3.47,
      "text": "negative one from zero to t, sorry, from"
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 446.76,
      "end": 450.67,
      "duration": 3.91,
      "text": "negative one"
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 452.47,
      "end": 452.48,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "to zero"
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 452.48,
      "end": 454.19,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "and takes on the value of plus one from"
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 454.2,
      "end": 459.39,
      "duration": 5.19,
      "text": "zero to one."
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 478.43,
      "end": 478.44,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay, so this is f of t."
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 478.44,
      "end": 480.75,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "This is t."
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 480.76,
      "end": 482.27,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "And"
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 482.28,
      "end": 488.07,
      "duration": 5.79,
      "text": "it transitions"
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 490.19,
      "end": 490.2,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "it makes its jumps"
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 490.2,
      "end": 492.23,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "at uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 492.24,
      "end": 495.39,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "the integers."
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 498.07,
      "end": 498.08,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So for example, uh it jumps from plus"
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 498.08,
      "end": 499.75,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "one to minus one at one"
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 499.76,
      "end": 501.95,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "and from plus one to minus one at minus"
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 501.96,
      "end": 504.55,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "one as well."
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 505.87,
      "end": 505.88,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And if I were to just quickly sketch the"
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 505.88,
      "end": 508.59,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "square wave function over top of it"
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 508.6,
      "end": 513.149,
      "duration": 4.549,
      "text": "or sorry, underneath of it"
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 514.19,
      "end": 514.2,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "the square wave function makes its"
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 514.2,
      "end": 518.35,
      "duration": 4.15,
      "text": "transitions"
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 520.87,
      "end": 520.88,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "at minus pi and pi."
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 520.88,
      "end": 524.47,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "So this is the square wave function."
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 530.83,
      "end": 530.84,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So we see that we can take the square"
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 530.84,
      "end": 533.67,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "wave function"
    },
    {
      "index": 185,
      "start": 535.55,
      "end": 535.56,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "and"
    },
    {
      "index": 186,
      "start": 535.56,
      "end": 537.11,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "squeeze it"
    },
    {
      "index": 187,
      "start": 537.12,
      "end": 539.35,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "to obtain this function f of t."
    },
    {
      "index": 188,
      "start": 539.36,
      "end": 541.23,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "And the question now is, what factor do"
    },
    {
      "index": 189,
      "start": 541.24,
      "end": 542.55,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "we have to squeeze the square wave"
    },
    {
      "index": 190,
      "start": 542.56,
      "end": 546.15,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "function by to get f of t?"
    },
    {
      "index": 191,
      "start": 546.16,
      "end": 549.03,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "Well, usually what I like to do is take"
    },
    {
      "index": 192,
      "start": 549.04,
      "end": 551.47,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "one characteristic point in the sketch"
    },
    {
      "index": 193,
      "start": 551.48,
      "end": 553.15,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "for in this case the square wave"
    },
    {
      "index": 194,
      "start": 553.16,
      "end": 555.11,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "function, so a nice characteristic point"
    },
    {
      "index": 195,
      "start": 555.12,
      "end": 556.31,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "is"
    },
    {
      "index": 196,
      "start": 556.32,
      "end": 558.15,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "when the square wave function has a"
    },
    {
      "index": 197,
      "start": 558.16,
      "end": 559.35,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "zero, so when it goes through the"
    },
    {
      "index": 198,
      "start": 559.36,
      "end": 562.31,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "origin, and compare it to the same"
    },
    {
      "index": 199,
      "start": 562.32,
      "end": 563.75,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "point"
    },
    {
      "index": 200,
      "start": 563.76,
      "end": 565.83,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "on this function f of t."
    },
    {
      "index": 201,
      "start": 565.84,
      "end": 568.67,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "So we see that the point pi has to get"
    },
    {
      "index": 202,
      "start": 568.68,
      "end": 571.83,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "stretched to the point one."
    },
    {
      "index": 203,
      "start": 571.84,
      "end": 573.95,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "So we we basically need to take the time"
    },
    {
      "index": 204,
      "start": 573.96,
      "end": 575.55,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "axis"
    },
    {
      "index": 205,
      "start": 575.56,
      "end": 577.79,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "in the square wave function and squeeze"
    },
    {
      "index": 206,
      "start": 577.8,
      "end": 584.07,
      "duration": 6.27,
      "text": "it by a factor of pi."
    },
    {
      "index": 207,
      "start": 586.55,
      "end": 586.56,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So what this means is that f of t is"
    },
    {
      "index": 208,
      "start": 586.56,
      "end": 589.51,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "going to be the square wave"
    },
    {
      "index": 209,
      "start": 589.52,
      "end": 591.23,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "and when we do what mathematicians"
    },
    {
      "index": 210,
      "start": 591.24,
      "end": 593.35,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "sometimes call a dilatation, a stretch"
    },
    {
      "index": 211,
      "start": 593.36,
      "end": 594.71,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "or a squeeze"
    },
    {
      "index": 212,
      "start": 594.72,
      "end": 597.15,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "if we're squeezing by some factor, That"
    },
    {
      "index": 213,
      "start": 597.16,
      "end": 599.03,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "factor always appears"
    },
    {
      "index": 214,
      "start": 599.04,
      "end": 599.79,
      "duration": 0.75,
      "text": "uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 215,
      "start": 599.8,
      "end": 602.19,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "in the argument of uh the function we're"
    },
    {
      "index": 216,
      "start": 602.2,
      "end": 603.59,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "squeezing."
    },
    {
      "index": 217,
      "start": 603.6,
      "end": 605.75,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "If it's a stretch, then it would be t"
    },
    {
      "index": 218,
      "start": 605.76,
      "end": 608.43,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "over the stretch factor."
    },
    {
      "index": 219,
      "start": 608.44,
      "end": 611.43,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "And we can quickly check here that if t"
    },
    {
      "index": 220,
      "start": 611.44,
      "end": 615.27,
      "duration": 3.83,
      "text": "uh equals 1, so as t goes from 0 to 1,"
    },
    {
      "index": 221,
      "start": 615.28,
      "end": 617.23,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "so when t is 1,"
    },
    {
      "index": 222,
      "start": 617.24,
      "end": 618.59,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "the square wave function is being"
    },
    {
      "index": 223,
      "start": 618.6,
      "end": 624.59,
      "duration": 5.99,
      "text": "evaluated at pi."
    },
    {
      "index": 224,
      "start": 625.87,
      "end": 625.88,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And I'll I'll now write out the Fourier"
    },
    {
      "index": 225,
      "start": 625.88,
      "end": 627.51,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "series. So, this is going to be 4 over"
    },
    {
      "index": 226,
      "start": 627.52,
      "end": 629.83,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "pi"
    },
    {
      "index": 227,
      "start": 629.84,
      "end": 634.83,
      "duration": 4.99,
      "text": "sum of n odd"
    },
    {
      "index": 228,
      "start": 637.47,
      "end": 637.48,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "1 over n"
    },
    {
      "index": 229,
      "start": 637.48,
      "end": 638.87,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "sin of"
    },
    {
      "index": 230,
      "start": 638.88,
      "end": 642.27,
      "duration": 3.39,
      "text": "n pi t."
    },
    {
      "index": 231,
      "start": 643.59,
      "end": 643.6,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And there's another quick check we can"
    },
    {
      "index": 232,
      "start": 643.6,
      "end": 644.59,
      "duration": 0.99,
      "text": "do."
    },
    {
      "index": 233,
      "start": 644.6,
      "end": 646.79,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "And that's uh this function f we were"
    },
    {
      "index": 234,
      "start": 646.8,
      "end": 649.23,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "told is 2 pi or sorry, is period uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 235,
      "start": 649.24,
      "end": 651.47,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "periodic with period 2."
    },
    {
      "index": 236,
      "start": 651.48,
      "end": 652.63,
      "duration": 1.15,
      "text": "And if we just take a look at this"
    },
    {
      "index": 237,
      "start": 652.64,
      "end": 654.19,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "function here, the Fourier series"
    },
    {
      "index": 238,
      "start": 654.2,
      "end": 657.03,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "representation of it, we see that"
    },
    {
      "index": 239,
      "start": 657.04,
      "end": 660.35,
      "duration": 3.31,
      "text": "each sin n pi t is in fact uh periodic"
    },
    {
      "index": 240,
      "start": 660.36,
      "end": 662.59,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "with period 2."
    },
    {
      "index": 241,
      "start": 662.6,
      "end": 663.91,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "So, that's just another quick uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 242,
      "start": 663.92,
      "end": 665.39,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "back-of-the-envelope check that we've"
    },
    {
      "index": 243,
      "start": 665.4,
      "end": 667.15,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "done our uh we've done our uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 244,
      "start": 667.16,
      "end": 669.51,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "calculation correctly."
    },
    {
      "index": 245,
      "start": 669.52,
      "end": 672.87,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "Okay, so this concludes part two."
    },
    {
      "index": 246,
      "start": 672.88,
      "end": 675.11,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "And then for lastly for part three,"
    },
    {
      "index": 247,
      "start": 675.12,
      "end": 677.03,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "f of t"
    },
    {
      "index": 248,
      "start": 677.04,
      "end": 679.35,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "is the absolute value of t from minus pi"
    },
    {
      "index": 249,
      "start": 679.36,
      "end": 681.31,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "to pi"
    },
    {
      "index": 250,
      "start": 681.32,
      "end": 683.43,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "and it's uh extended beyond minus pi to"
    },
    {
      "index": 251,
      "start": 683.44,
      "end": 685.47,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "pi uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 252,
      "start": 685.48,
      "end": 687.39,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "to make it 2 pi periodic."
    },
    {
      "index": 253,
      "start": 687.4,
      "end": 688.75,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "And at first it might look like this"
    },
    {
      "index": 254,
      "start": 688.76,
      "end": 690.35,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "function f of t"
    },
    {
      "index": 255,
      "start": 690.36,
      "end": 691.67,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "is not related to the square wave"
    },
    {
      "index": 256,
      "start": 691.68,
      "end": 693.829,
      "duration": 2.149,
      "text": "function."
    },
    {
      "index": 257,
      "start": 693.839,
      "end": 696.07,
      "duration": 2.231,
      "text": "But if we look at it a little more"
    },
    {
      "index": 258,
      "start": 696.08,
      "end": 697.27,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "carefully"
    },
    {
      "index": 259,
      "start": 697.28,
      "end": 699.35,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "and say analyze the derivative of f of"
    },
    {
      "index": 260,
      "start": 699.36,
      "end": 700.829,
      "duration": 1.469,
      "text": "t,"
    },
    {
      "index": 261,
      "start": 700.839,
      "end": 702.39,
      "duration": 1.551,
      "text": "we see that this function takes on the"
    },
    {
      "index": 262,
      "start": 702.4,
      "end": 704.15,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "value of plus one"
    },
    {
      "index": 263,
      "start": 704.16,
      "end": 706.27,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "on the interval 0 to pi and takes on the"
    },
    {
      "index": 264,
      "start": 706.28,
      "end": 708.11,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "value of minus one on the interval of"
    },
    {
      "index": 265,
      "start": 708.12,
      "end": 711.91,
      "duration": 3.79,
      "text": "minus pi to 0."
    },
    {
      "index": 266,
      "start": 714.51,
      "end": 714.52,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And this is exactly"
    },
    {
      "index": 267,
      "start": 714.52,
      "end": 717.39,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "the square wave."
    },
    {
      "index": 268,
      "start": 719.39,
      "end": 719.4,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So, what we can do is we can write f of"
    },
    {
      "index": 269,
      "start": 719.4,
      "end": 721.15,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "t"
    },
    {
      "index": 270,
      "start": 721.16,
      "end": 722.99,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "it's going to be an integral"
    },
    {
      "index": 271,
      "start": 723.0,
      "end": 730.71,
      "duration": 7.71,
      "text": "of the square wave function."
    },
    {
      "index": 272,
      "start": 732.51,
      "end": 732.52,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "So, specifically,"
    },
    {
      "index": 273,
      "start": 732.52,
      "end": 734.35,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "we have the integral of"
    },
    {
      "index": 274,
      "start": 734.36,
      "end": 737.59,
      "duration": 3.23,
      "text": "square wave"
    },
    {
      "index": 275,
      "start": 739.75,
      "end": 739.76,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "which is going to be the integral of"
    },
    {
      "index": 276,
      "start": 739.76,
      "end": 742.11,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "4 over pi"
    },
    {
      "index": 277,
      "start": 742.12,
      "end": 744.27,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "1 over n"
    },
    {
      "index": 278,
      "start": 744.28,
      "end": 751.11,
      "duration": 6.83,
      "text": "sin n t."
    },
    {
      "index": 279,
      "start": 760.63,
      "end": 760.64,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And I'm going to leave this as an"
    },
    {
      "index": 280,
      "start": 760.64,
      "end": 762.31,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "indefinite integral."
    },
    {
      "index": 281,
      "start": 762.32,
      "end": 763.31,
      "duration": 0.99,
      "text": "So, when we integrate, we have a"
    },
    {
      "index": 282,
      "start": 763.32,
      "end": 765.55,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "constant of integration"
    },
    {
      "index": 283,
      "start": 765.56,
      "end": 768.55,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "c"
    },
    {
      "index": 284,
      "start": 769.829,
      "end": 769.839,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "plus"
    },
    {
      "index": 285,
      "start": 769.839,
      "end": 772.55,
      "duration": 2.711,
      "text": "4 over pi"
    },
    {
      "index": 286,
      "start": 772.56,
      "end": 773.91,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "sum"
    },
    {
      "index": 287,
      "start": 773.92,
      "end": 777.15,
      "duration": 3.23,
      "text": "of 1 over n squared"
    },
    {
      "index": 288,
      "start": 777.16,
      "end": 784.19,
      "duration": 7.03,
      "text": "and we have negative cosine n t."
    },
    {
      "index": 289,
      "start": 789.15,
      "end": 789.16,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "index": 290,
      "start": 789.16,
      "end": 791.55,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "And now we have one last uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 291,
      "start": 791.56,
      "end": 793.59,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "question to answer."
    },
    {
      "index": 292,
      "start": 793.6,
      "end": 796.19,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "What is the constant of integration?"
    },
    {
      "index": 293,
      "start": 796.2,
      "end": 797.19,
      "duration": 0.99,
      "text": "Well, notice how the constant of"
    },
    {
      "index": 294,
      "start": 797.2,
      "end": 799.59,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "integration can be identified with the"
    },
    {
      "index": 295,
      "start": 799.6,
      "end": 802.59,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "a0 term of the Fourier series."
    },
    {
      "index": 296,
      "start": 802.6,
      "end": 803.99,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "So, if we want the constant of"
    },
    {
      "index": 297,
      "start": 804.0,
      "end": 805.91,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "integration, we can just calculate it"
    },
    {
      "index": 298,
      "start": 805.92,
      "end": 808.79,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "directly by the integral formula for the"
    },
    {
      "index": 299,
      "start": 808.8,
      "end": 810.99,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "a0 uh"
    },
    {
      "index": 300,
      "start": 811.0,
      "end": 812.39,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "of this function."
    },
    {
      "index": 301,
      "start": 812.4,
      "end": 814.51,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "So, what this means is c"
    },
    {
      "index": 302,
      "start": 814.52,
      "end": 817.95,
      "duration": 3.43,
      "text": "is going to be 1 over 2 pi"
    },
    {
      "index": 303,
      "start": 817.96,
      "end": 819.03,
      "duration": 1.07,
      "text": "Essentially, it's just the average of"
    },
    {
      "index": 304,
      "start": 819.04,
      "end": 821.03,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "the function, but it's pi to pi the"
    },
    {
      "index": 305,
      "start": 821.04,
      "end": 827.87,
      "duration": 6.83,
      "text": "absolute value of t"
    },
    {
      "index": 306,
      "start": 841.15,
      "end": 841.16,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "index": 307,
      "start": 841.16,
      "end": 843.03,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "So, just to quickly recap,"
    },
    {
      "index": 308,
      "start": 843.04,
      "end": 844.51,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "in this problem we were given several"
    },
    {
      "index": 309,
      "start": 844.52,
      "end": 846.15,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "functions which were related to the"
    },
    {
      "index": 310,
      "start": 846.16,
      "end": 847.87,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "square wave function"
    },
    {
      "index": 311,
      "start": 847.88,
      "end": 849.95,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "and we started off knowing what the"
    },
    {
      "index": 312,
      "start": 849.96,
      "end": 851.15,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "Fourier series for the square wave"
    },
    {
      "index": 313,
      "start": 851.16,
      "end": 852.63,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "function was."
    },
    {
      "index": 314,
      "start": 852.64,
      "end": 855.03,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "And by manipulating uh or rewriting"
    },
    {
      "index": 315,
      "start": 855.04,
      "end": 856.59,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "these functions in terms of the square"
